Article 5

The Regional Government is responsible for efforts to protect women and children from acts of violence in the form of:
a. physical violence;
b. sexual violence;
c. economic violence;
d. social violence;
e. psychological violence;
f. domestic neglect;
g. coercion or deprivation of liberty; andh. threats of certain actions.

Article 8

1. The Regional Government shall prevent acts of violence against women and children by:a. socializing laws and regulations; b. providing counseling/guidance;
c. providing education on the dangers of domestic violence; d. conducting seminars/workshops or the like;
e. establishing work networks in efforts to prevent violence; f. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
g. establishing a violence prevention system, mapping locations or areas prone to violence;andh. increasing public awareness in behaving in accordance with religious norms.
2. In addition to carrying out prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), prevention of acts of violence against children shall also be carried out by increasing family capacity in child protection and parenting skills.
3. In addition to the Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is obliged to be implemented by:a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. community;
c. educational institutions;
d. health institutions;
e. social community institutions;
f. Desa pakraman; and jdih.bulelengkab.go.idg. business world and other institutions.

Article 22

MSS as referred to in Article 21 has performance indicators including:
a. coverage of Women and Child Victims of Violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers in integrated service units;
b. coverage of Women and Child Victims of Violence who receive health services by trained health workers at Community Health Centers and Hospitals;
c. coverage of Social Rehabilitation services provided by trained Social Rehabilitation officers for Women and Child Victims of Violence in integrated service units;
d. coverage of spiritual guidance services provided by trained spiritual guidance officers for Women and Child Victims of Violence in integrated service units;
e. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level to court decisions on cases of Violence against Women and Children;
f. coverage of Women and Child Victims of Violence who receive legal aid services;
g. coverage of Repatriation services for Women and Child Victims of Violence; andh. coverage of social reintegration services for Women and Child Victims of Violence.

REGENT OF BULELENG,

Considering:
a. that every citizen has the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of violence that degrade human dignity;
b. that women and children are vulnerable groups who tend to experience violence, therefore they need to receive optimal protection;
c. that based on the provisions of Article 12 paragraph (2) letter b of Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government as has been amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, women's empowerment and child protection constitute mandatory government affairs for regional governments;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children From Acts of Violence;

In View of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 69 of 1958 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions within the Level I Regions of Bali, West Nusa Tenggara and East Nusa Tenggara (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia jdih.bulelengkab.go.id Year 1958 Number 122, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1655);
3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as has been amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
6. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
7. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning the Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);
8. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587); as has been amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number jdih.bulelengkab.go.id 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
9. Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2016 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);
10. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
11. Government Regulation Number 9 of 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);
12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Women's Protection;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;
14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Women and Child Victims of Violence;
15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Women and Child Victims of Violence;
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;

