CHAPTER III

RIGHTS OF VICTIMS

Article 4

Every Woman and Child Victim of Violence has the right:
a. to be respected for their dignity as human beings;

jdih.bulelengkab.go.id
b. to receive Protection from family, community, Regional Government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on a court protection order;
c. to physical, psychological and sexual health recovery according to the suffering experienced by victims of violence;
d. to special handling related to the confidentiality of Victims; e. to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
f. to spiritual guidance services; andg. to settlement through mediation, if it is the best solution for the interests of the victim; andh. to determine their own decisions.

Article 14

1. The Regional Government shall conduct cooperation and coordination in order to ensure the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence;
2. Cooperation and coordination as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus that administer governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.

Article 16

1. In certain circumstances the Regional Government may cooperate with:a. other regional governments;
b. police;
c. advocates;
d. health workers;

jdih.bulelengkab.go.id
e. social workers;
f. volunteer assistants;
g. spiritual counselors;
h. other law enforcers, to assist victims in court proceedings;
i. national commission on violence against women;
j. Indonesian child protection commission or child protection institutions;and/orak. certain parties desired for the benefit of the victim. (2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) may take the form of: a. socialization;
b. provision of legal aid;
c. health services;
d. victim assistance;
e. counseling;
f. social rehabilitation;
g. spiritual guidance;and/orah. repatriation and social reintegration.

Article 17

1. The Regent coordinates the protection of women and children from acts of violence with:a. the government;
b. provincial government;
c. vertical agencies;
d. educational institutions;ande. community institutions.
2. Coordination as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. religious affairs;
b. health affairs;
c. education affairs;
d. social affairs;
e. legal affairs; andf. manpower affairs.

jdih.bulelengkab.go.id

Article 5

The Regional Government is responsible for efforts to protect women and children from acts of violence in the form of:
a. physical violence;
b. sexual violence;
c. economic violence;
d. social violence;
e. psychological violence;
f. domestic neglect;
g. coercion or deprivation of liberty; andh. threats of certain actions.

Article 8

1. The Regional Government shall prevent acts of violence against women and children by:a. socializing laws and regulations; b. providing counseling/guidance;
c. providing education on the dangers of domestic violence; d. conducting seminars/workshops or the like;
e. establishing work networks in efforts to prevent violence; f. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
g. establishing a violence prevention system, mapping locations or areas prone to violence;andh. increasing public awareness in behaving in accordance with religious norms.
2. In addition to carrying out prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), prevention of acts of violence against children shall also be carried out by increasing family capacity in child protection and parenting skills.
3. In addition to the Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is obliged to be implemented by:a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. community;
c. educational institutions;
d. health institutions;
e. social community institutions;
f. Desa pakraman; and jdih.bulelengkab.go.idg. business world and other institutions.

