Article 22

MSS as referred to in Article 21 has performance indicators including:
a. coverage of Women and Child Victims of Violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers in integrated service units;
b. coverage of Women and Child Victims of Violence who receive health services by trained health workers at Community Health Centers and Hospitals;
c. coverage of Social Rehabilitation services provided by trained Social Rehabilitation officers for Women and Child Victims of Violence in integrated service units;
d. coverage of spiritual guidance services provided by trained spiritual guidance officers for Women and Child Victims of Violence in integrated service units;
e. coverage of law enforcement from the investigation level to court decisions on cases of Violence against Women and Children;
f. coverage of Women and Child Victims of Violence who receive legal aid services;
g. coverage of Repatriation services for Women and Child Victims of Violence; andh. coverage of social reintegration services for Women and Child Victims of Violence.

Article 11

1. The Regional Government shall implement integrated services for victims of acts of violence through activities:a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. counseling;
d. spiritual guidance;
e. social rehabilitation services;
f. legal aid and assistance services; andg. repatriation and reintegration.
2. Services as referred to in paragraph (1) must be supported by facilities in the form of:a. special service rooms within the police force;
b. expert and professional personnel;
c. service centers and safe houses;and/ord. other facilities and infrastructure needed for victim recovery. (3) Services as referred to in paragraph (1), including the preparation of visum et repertum, shall be carried out free of charge.

jdih.bulelengkab.go.id (4) The provision of services to victims of acts of violence shall be carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government together with P2TP2A with other social institutions;

5. P2TP2A and other social institutions as referred to in paragraph (4) may receive and send case referrals from other service units in a networked manner;
6. Integrated services for victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2), paragraph (3) and paragraph (4) shall be implemented in accordance with Standard Operating Procedures;
7. Provisions regarding Standard Operating Procedures as referred to in paragraph (6) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 15

1. The Regional Government in the context of services for victims of acts of violence against women and children, shall establish P2TP2A;
2. P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall function as: a. information center for women and children;
b. service center for women and children who are victims of violence; and c. empowerment center for women and children.
3. P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) is obliged to: a. provide services as quickly as possible and free of charge to witnesses and/or victims;

jdih.bulelengkab.go.id
b. provide protection and fulfillment of the rights of witnesses and/or victims to health rehabilitation, social rehabilitation, repatriation, social reintegration and legal aid;
c. cooperate with certain institutions in providing translators and volunteer assistants needed for witnesses and/or victims;
d. establish networks with government or private hospitals for treatment and health recovery of victims and cooperate with witness and victim protection institutions, social protection houses or government-owned trauma centers, community or other institutions for victim health recovery.  e. provide convenience, comfort, and safety for witnesses and/or victims;
f. maintain confidentiality of witnesses and/or victims;
g. provide fulfillment of legal aid for witnesses and/or victims; andh. in the event that integrated service provision is carried out in a networked manner, be responsible for the entire referral process of services needed by victims.
4. P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall have the duties to: a. provide integrated services to victims of violence; and b. provide protection to victims of acts of violence, reporters and witnesses.
5. The provision of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (4) letter a shall be implemented in accordance with Standard Operating Procedures established by the Regional Government.
6. The appointment of P2TP2A management as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by Regent Decree.

